From 9c7082d2d1c3aabd0c5301fe020ccb0890faea3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Calogero Mandracchia <calogero@efebia.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:54:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] mcp: pass session and thread ids to stdio servers that
 ask for them

A stdio MCP server can now request the identity of the chat that starts
it, with the same values shell commands receive:

    env_vars = [
      { name = "CODEX_SESSION_ID", source = "codex" },
      { name = "CODEX_THREAD_ID", source = "codex" },
    ]

`source = "codex"` is accepted only for these two names. Their values are
never read from the Codex process environment. Servers started outside a
thread get neither variable, and a pooled connection is never shared
between threads that requested different ids.
